[h2]Greetings, Void Hunters![/h2]

We hope you have been enjoying our latest major update, [b]Hammer Time![/b] Over the last few days, thanks to your reports and help, we managed to find a few issues with the game that we felt needed a hotfix update to make sure the game is as smooth as it can be!

Here is the [b]full list of changes released today, with Hotfix 1.2d1,[/b] and also a few that had been fixed already a few days ago!

[list]
[*]Fixed a critical issue that would cause combat text to break in multiple languages (patched one hour after the main update);
[*]Fixed an issue where even at 0 visibility, special effects for certain projectiles (such as Electrified) would still be simulated, leading to massive slowdown. Turning the effect visibility to 0 should now grant a much better performance boost, for example when using the Blacksmith's with his special weapon skill;
[*]Fixed an issue where in extreme scenarios Weapon Summon skills would only use their special attack, when their attack speed was too high. Same fix applied for the Spellblade's artifact power, which had the same problem;
[*]Fixed an issue where the summons created by Blacksmith's weapons would not be moved inside a Titan room, being locked out for the fight;
[*]Fixed a silent exception with the Plague Viper which would cause performance degradation;
[*]Fixed a couple of issues with the Blacksmith's voice over not having the correct subtitles (or no subtitles);
[*]Fixed an issue where the Chaotic trait would not properly combine different power ups, causing it to not work as intended if you collected power ups from different Titans that improved chaotic;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Barbarian's summoned weapons would not properly use Whirlwind;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Captain's summoned weapons would have Gunpowder, which is not supported for summons;
[*]Fixed an issue where Chaotic Swirl would not have the proper power up modifiers, replacing Summon Quantity for Multicast, which works as intended;
[*]Fixed the tooltip for the Legionnaire Ascension power up for increased duration;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Savage Pact rune would have no text in most languages;
[*]Fixed which soundtracks are used for the Titan Hunt desert maps, which were pointing for the incorrect tracks;
[*]Fixed multiple small localization issues in different languages;
[/list]

Hopefully these fixes will make your experience better and if you run into any other issues, do let us know, as we continue to work on the next update!

[b]Thank you very much for your support,[/b]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/0613ae8b16cc071c726ac24a6c6e0f9156b2c8a2.gif[/img]

[b][i]~ Soulstone Survivors team[/i][/b]

[h3]Greetings, Void Hunters![/h3]

[b]It’s hammer time![/b] We have just released [b]update 1.2 for Soulstone Survivors,[/b] and this is a special one, which not only introduces [b]new legendary weapons, new map, titan, power-ups… but also a new powerful Void Hunter![/b]
[previewyoutube=JI8OqNKMHBs;full][/previewyoutube]

[h2]New Void Hunter - The Blacksmith[/h2]
If you want a job well done, you gotta do it yourself! [b]The Blacksmith[/b] joins the frey with a unique playstyle. He [b]does NOT have access to any of the general skills[/b] in the game, instead he is able to [b]summon weapons from ANY character in the game to fight for him![/b]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/3c6f90155a01a3c2fafbd8557e41daa130957cee.png[/img]
This bonus character is a reward for the most dedicated Void Hunters, who have [b]completed all 22 skill trees[/b] in the game, and offers a unique twist!

[h2]New Legendary Weapons[/h2]
This update introduces the Legendary Weapons for the [b]Arcane Weaver[/b], [b]Sentinel[/b], [b]Paladin[/b] and [b]Chaoswalker[/b], with new powerful skills and synergies to be explored!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/b3ae9ae80f276c9f8db7988ca54b0ab909ad54c1.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/3bb893b67af781575de0d1ef73edab2dee7ca355.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/69ba45a43a8f5de7848c9896cd5202d45b78e3ec.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/c63b7daa3bd72901eb19dd1f6d66675a312df734.png[/img]

[h2]New Map - Sporewilds[/h2]
Venture into this new Titan Hunt area and bring an end to the infected creatures of the Sporewilds!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/ecebf25de5c6e33194ffd25c08b3dec4f6b65e24.png[/img]

[h2]New Titan - Fellipox, the Fungal Abomination[/h2]
Unlock new power ups by defeating this powerful Titan, with new and powerful synergies for different builds!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/ff3684147e3934c290517d9a5d3db70da1cb65eb.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/65ca5475779ed9e24eeec83742471eca3db2b0da.png[/img]

[h2]General improvements and fixes:[/h2]
[list]
[*]Combat text reworked from the ground up for much better performance;
[*]Added new information card that appears the first time you go into Endless or Overlord mode, that highlights the existence of the special effect visibility slider;
[*]New soundtrack added for “Cave-themed” maps, such as the Caves of Dhal Zhog, Broodmother's Lair and Kobold Mines;
[*]Re-worked Icy Veins, which no longer fires projectiles at random targets around you, but instead launches projectiles that orbit around you;
[*]Added new sound option to disable the Experience collecting sound;
[*]Considerably improved the Cursed Captain’s and Myrmidon’s artifact powers to require less stacks of Artifact Power and have increased power;
[*]Update Smite visuals for faster performance;
[*]Updated the functionality of Quicksand so that it has considerably better performance;
[*]Adjusted the area indicator for the tornadoes created by Mhyzahet (Scorpion titan);
[*]Radiant Cracks (Midorahk power up) now synergises from Exposed to Radiance, changed from Fragility to Radiance;
[*]Chaotic is now able to launch more than one bonus skill if its chance to trigger is over 100%;
[*]Improved Savage Pact rune description to show what is the maximum health you need for the maximum bonus;
[*]Added more details to the tooltips of multiple skills, describing durations, quantity of projectiles, etc where needed;
[*]Fixed an animation issue with the Shaman where some parts of the character would stretch weirdly;
[*]Fixed an animation issue where the Shaman could potentially stay dancing forever after his ascension;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Titan Hunt sigils would not be interactable if the Assassin artifact power was active;
[*]Fixed a possible issue with player collision against the Titan Hunt barriers;
[*]Fixed a small issue with the Myrmidon skill tree were a specific node was incorrectly set up;
[*]Fixed a rare issue with the completion of the “All Skill Trees” achievement not completing, even after all characters are completed;
[*]Fixed an issue where multiple skills would not deal damage to small spiders if you had a low enough area of effect;
[*]Fixed an issue where Resonating Crystal would not deal damage properly to every enemy;
[*]Fixed an issue where the hidden achievements could show a random tooltip when hovered;
[*]Fixed an issue with the Unholy Cathedral unique power ups when you use the Quality Standards rune;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Voice Over system could throw exceptions in a very specific scenario;
[/list]

We hope you enjoy the update and have a good time with the Blacksmith! As always, [b]thank you very much for your support[/b] along the way and stay tuned for there is still more to come!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/0613ae8b16cc071c726ac24a6c6e0f9156b2c8a2.gif[/img]

[b][i]~ Soulstone Survivors team[/i][/b]

[h3]Greetings, Void Hunters![/h3]

Today we come to you with the first post-release update for Soulstone Survivors, [b]the Golden Burglar![/b] This update is just the first of many! Sit tight, enjoy a nice cup of coffee and let's get into whats new!

[h2]New Legendary Weapons[/h2]
You can now craft the Legendary Weapons for the [b]Barbarian[/b], [b]Pyromancer[/b], [b]Hound Master[/b] and [b]Spellblade![/b] These are the first 4 coming to the game, with new powerful skills and synergies to be explored!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/486ec10f8a4f5a171ee71bad07cdbf298843e8ce.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/ae98141c9d9c3cdaca165752e13652a268706bae.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/3c3967941fc31bb0a46df60224d060ab0b6dcb6b.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/683e5743b4784ada26e9c6ea37c0634b9ef5febd.png[/img]

[h2]New Map - Tomb of the Sun God[/h2]
Available in the Titan Hunt, explore the tomb and dig through its secrets, and defeat its ancient guardian...
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/2ae5597e5edc8dbddab4097b6cba5ea37c4ee69e.png[/img]

[h2]New Titan - Midorahk, the Golden Burglar[/h2]
Face this new powerful Titan and unlock new unique power ups that can elevate your builds to the next level!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/2785ea3252efccbae29ae505639816a13f988af0.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/c274868c13bb7afb30fc23de326b62c55b8abbe7.png[/img]

[h2]Updated Visuals - Frozen Wastelands[/h2]
A much needed face lift to bring this map more in line with our newer scenarios!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/bc788681e7f0122cd831dc8b61e637f0d3c2cd1c.png[/img]

[h2]General improvements and fixes:[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subtitles are now localized into all languages, along with multiple fixes across the game;
[*]Implemented a way to skip Titan Hunt cutscenes for Titan introductions and Void King scenes;
[*]New map icons for all Void Fields maps;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Skill Tree would show all nodes as “possible to upgrade” when you first open it, only being fixed after you try to purchase a node;
[*]Added a slider to the Settings where you can control the opacity level of the minimap;
[*]Fixed an issue where it would be possible to inspect the skills of your first weapon in the Blacksmith if you did not have any more weapons unlocked;
[*]Fixed an issue where the game could become locked if you surrendered before opening the Primordial Portal in the Titan Hunt;
[*]Fixed an issue where the sensitivy of the scrolling in the Mastery Runes UI was too quick;
[*]Multiple performance fixes and adjustments across the game;
[*]Fixed an issue where if you opened the Level Up Screen at a very specific time when going through a Titan Hunt portal would lead the game to be soft locked;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Vial of Titan Blood would be transparent if you kept going without going to the Primordial Portal;
[*]Fixed an issue where your minions would scale much more than intended in the Titan Hunt especially in higher difficulties;
[*]Fixed an issue where most melee minions would scale less than intended with attack speed, and should now attack faster especially in late game scenarios;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Swift Execution rune would give multiplicative bonus critical damage based on your movement speed, instead of additive, being way stronger than intended;
[*]Fixed the minimap in the Netherworld which had a few details missing;
[*]Fixed an issue where depending on your skills it would be impossible to destroy minerals and health crystals;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Hound Master’s dogs would not receive buffs such as Radiance, Prowess, etc;
[*]Elemental Power rune bonus is now multiplicative instead of additive, which was the intended effect;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Chaos Golem description would not mention the Stun that your summons can cause;
[*]Fixed an issue where a couple of the Legionnaire’s artifact powers were not applying the appropriate negative effects;
[*]Chaos Stabilizer rune now grants 10 purity on Chaotic procs, up from 2;
[*]Increased the rotation speed for most Titans;
[/list]

We hope that you have been enjoying the game so far, and well... let's just say [b]we are cooking a little surprise for you all in our next major update[/b]... so stay tunned, for there's still quite a bit coming, and as always, [b]thank you so much for your amazing support!![/b]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/0613ae8b16cc071c726ac24a6c6e0f9156b2c8a2.gif[/img]

[b][i]~ Soulstone Survivors team[/i][/b]

[h3]Greetings, Void Hunters![/h3]

We have just released [b]Hotfix Update 1.0g2[/b], which solves a bunch of the issues reported over the last few days! This update would not be possible without your support and feedback, so [b]thank you for helping us make the game as smooth as it can be![/b]

[h2]General changes:[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Minor change to Vsync option in graphics settings:[/b] Due to an error in our migration process for some users, Vsync was automatically disabled. With this hotfix update, it will be enabled again by default, so if you would like it turned off, please change the setting in the Graphic settings menu. You will now have another option which allows you to set any FPS cap you like with a slider for full flexibility;
[*]Fixed an issue where Warcry (Barbarian Artifact Power) would grant buffs but not cause damage on enemies, being a lot less effective than intended;
[*]Considerably reduced the effective health and area of effect of Shadow Lords of the Void;
[*]Corrupted Void Hunter bosses have had their areas reduced, either with smaller size, longer cooldown or in general would use less of the arena;
[*]Reduced effective health of the Void King, especially in the last stage of the fight;
[*]Fixed an issue where certain Corrupted Void Hunter skills would be affected by the visibility slider, becoming hard to see if visibility was set too low;
[*]Fixed an issue where ascensions and other objects could spawn inside the Void King in phase 1 of the fight, making them impossible to interact with until phase 1 was over;
[*]Fixed an issue where on a Gamepad it would not be possible to change the difficulty of the Unholy Cathedral’s last ritual;
[*]Fixed an issue where using Mouse movement + dashing could cause small step-backs in the wrong direction;
[*]Gunpowder is now affected by runes that reduce the amount of Ammunition required per proc;
[*]Fixed an issue where a couple of Samurai’s Ascension power ups did not have a pick-up limit, which should be limited to 5;
[*]Fixed an issue where Lords of the Void could spawn in a very weird place in the Caves of Dhal Zhog;
[*]Fixed an issue where there would be an unintended delay before Mh’thaeus fight in the Unholy Cathedral, causing a few issues with ascensions;
[*]Fixed an issue where in lower resolutions it would not be possible to filter the Profile screens by character;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Monkey King model would become… wonky with certain skills;
[*]Fixed an issue where the visuals of certain locked characters would display incorrectly, with a big black square;
[*]Fixed multiple localization issues across the game (International subtitles are still being worked on and will be here soon!);
[*]Fixed an issue where in extreme late game scenarios certain projectiles would not hit enemies properly, causing less damage than intended;
[*]Changed Ammo Box visuals to be less intrusive;
[*]Fixed an issue where skills such as “Shredding Armor” (chance to gain a certain buff over the duration) would not properly count when they give you the buff. This is relevant if you have power ups such as Huntress Snare, from Aruanak, which launches a skill when a certain number of stacks of Aptitude is applied;
[*]Changed the visuals of Dragonflight so that the actual dragon is more noticeable (but still affected by the visibility slider);
[*]Fixed scenario objects not properly dissolving when destroyed;
[/list]

[h3][b]PS: International localization for subtitles is still coming! We are almost there and will make another hotfix update as soon as they are available![/b][/h3]

We hope you are enjoying the full release, and keep an eye out, [b]for we have not uncovered everything that hides in the void just yet...[/b]

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/b59ee068423a08c66b49b83b7fe9d8fb7853a631.gif[/img]

[i][b]~ Soulstone Survivors team[/b][/i]

[h3]Greetings, Void Hunters![/h3]

The day has finally come… [b]Soulstone Survivors is now officially out of Early Access[/b], along with a [b]HUGE[/b] release update! We’ve prepared a special trailer for the occasion:
[previewyoutube=_9i8pLpFO-U;full][/previewyoutube]
This update brings new characters, skills, artifact powers, and of course… new lore with full voice over support across the game! If you'd like a quick overview of the key points coming in this update, check out our video below:
[previewyoutube=c32u5Aoz_Go;full][/previewyoutube]

[h2]Lore, The Voices of the Void and the Void King[/h2]
To bring context to the world and the mission and culture of the Void Hunters, we are introducing a new introduction experience, along with over 2500 voice lines spread across the game to bring personality to each hunter.
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/6ea224846b0af33d8266f1b3548df947f2697de2.png[/img]
This is more than just an introduction as this new content introduces 7 new bosses, new unique powers, a new map, the Netherworld, and the final chapter where you will face off against the Void King himself!

[h3][i][b]Important note:[/b] Unfortunately subtitles are not fully localized yet and will appear in English regardless of the chosen language. These are activelly being worked on and will be ready in the coming weeks, we apologise for the inconvenience and will get them in the game as soon as possible![/i][/h3]

[h2]Titan Hunt - Part 2[/h2]
This update brings the conclusion to the Titan Hunt chapter within the game, where you will finally learn what you can use Titan Blood for, face new challenges and learn new, unique powers.
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/2043fe0ae52b355c6f0e1a59ec60dda730307fd6.png[/img]

[h2]New Character: The Machinist[/h2]
Having mastered the ways of the Soulstones, [b]the Machinist[/b] uses his brilliance to create powerful machinery harvesting the energy from these unstable crystals. With his battle armor he specializes in [b]focused beams of energy[/b] to destroy powerful foes and [b]large area damage[/b] to cut through waves of enemies.

His weapons bring a set of new powers into the game, and with his ascension he’s able to harvest [b]charged soulstones to awaken the Machine Spirit, launching a devasting blast![/b]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/152f27672006ba158de0bf08373e5f8ec6875176.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/da44f99fdf388bdf75459ea468c4a252530f9bd6.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/cf4f3de0cfd3cdff42d126e82ece4a1d8b739232.png[/img]

[h2]New Character: The Samurai[/h2]
After decades of discipline and training, [b]the Samurai[/b] has learned not only how to fight his demons, but control them to unleash chaos upon his enemies. Like his predecessors, he is one with the blade, but he unites the old and the new, being capable of [b]unleashing powerful strikes channelling elemental powers against his foes.[/b]

Each of his Katanas is designed for different combat techniques, and when all hope is lost, the Samurai may [b]materialize his own rage to decimate any that stands in his way.[/b]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/a162eb49bc9f6e94d6dfdfaceb3d240d6fe2f7ff.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/885ddb5044a32d62f6097b71739c8876cf25c506.png[/img]
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/99fc84d2ac4f1ac8756748e476f6400c561885cd.png[/img]

[h2]New Artifact Powers[/h2]
This update also brings the artifact powers for [b]all remaining 12 characters![/b] Upgrade your weapons to the Artifact rarity and gain access to these [b]powerful skills that compliment the playstyles of each character[/b] and offer another way to enhance your builds to the next level!
[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/94f5cccc993b6251201e85f796b75edd42cddb8d.png[/img]

[h2]General changes:[/h2]
[list]
[*](Finally) Added option to toggle all curses in a tier with a single button;
[*]Added functionality for Mouse Only mode to always follow the cursor (can be toggled in the options menu);
[*]Added option to Mouse-Only mode for your character to always move towards your cursor (without the need for clicking to move);
[*]Added small lore descriptions to each game mode;
[*]Considerably increased the amount of prestige and minerals earned in the Titan Hunt;
[*]Titans now drop up to 20 legendary void essences when defeated, if playing on a high enough difficulty level;
[*]Radiance, Electric and Icy Veins now require considerably less stacks to be used;
[*]Your health is now automatically recovered when you open the door to a Titan;
[*]Titan Hunt difficulties and blood levels now have lower scaling for enemy damage, attack speed and movement speed;
[*]Fixed an issue where Aruanak (Titan) had an attack causing damage in a large area, causing invisible damage;
[*]Allaxis now spawns less grenades with his special attack;
[*]Fixed a rare issue where a character could become “locked” again due to save inconsistencies;
[*]Fixed an issue where at times, special portals would not appear (from completing special events);
[*]Fixed an issue where soulstones that were not manually collected in the Titan Hunt would not work properly with the Material Harvest rune, yielding less materials than intended;
[*]Fixed a rare issue where Doom would attempt to execute a target, but not cause the expected damage;
[*]Treasure Bug will not longer appear in the Void Fields, only in the Titan Hunt;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Hound Master’s ascension could show inconsistent numbers for the level of your dogs;
[*]Fixed an issue where the minimap would not update when fighting in the second stage of the Unholy Cathedral;[*]Fixed an issue with some fonts for Polish and Turkish versions;
[*]Fixed an issue with Appearances UI scroll list;
[*]Fixed a graphical issue in certain graphics cards and platforms that would cause visual effects to glitch weirdly;
[*]Fixed an issue where the minimap would appear if you unpaused the game during a level up screen;
[*]Multiple minor UI fixes and improvements across the game;
[/list]

[h2]Hotfix 1.0g (18/06/2025, 20:50 UTC):[/h2]
[list]
[*]Fixed a critical issue where multiple visual effects were not being displayed properly on Linux (and Steam Deck);
[*]Fixed an issue where Restart/Surrender could lead to exceptions, making the game unstable and not working as intended, especially in the first few times playing the game;
[*]Fixed an issue where Weapon crafting achievements for the Machinist and Samurai were not properly propagated to Steam;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Corrupt Arcane Weaver at times would not appear, when playing on the Sigil of the Void in Titan Hunt mode;
[*]Fixed an issue where certain Summon skills would not be able to properly damage the Void King in Stage 1;
[*]Fixed an issue where Beam skills (such as Arcane Beam and others) would not be able to damage the Void King properly;
[*]Fixed an issue where a few enemies would cause damage in an area slightly larger than the red areas;
[*]Fixed the description of Chromatic Slash, which should say Damaging Effects;
[*]Fixed an issue in the Kobold Mines where in extreme situations the player could be pushed outside of the boss area;
[*]Fixed the tooltips of achievements without reward showing incorrectly;
[*]Added the Earth and Frontal tags to Chromatic Slash;
[*]Fixed multiple localization issues in subtitles and otherwise (international subtitles still not in place);
[*]Fixed version label in the top left of the screen to no longer say "Early Access";
[/list]

[h2]Through the Dawnstone, we ascend![/h2]
It’s still hard to believe we are finally here. Working on Soulstone Survivors so far has been a journey like no other, a once in a lifetime experience that I cannot believe how lucky I am to have had, [b]and I can say from the bottom of my heart, THANK YOU![/b] There is still much to come to the game, the new legendary weapons, new bosses and maps for the Titan Hunt, and even new secrets… but we could not be happier with the [b]game that we, us from Game Smithing and YOU, the community, have built together.[/b]

We wouldn’t be here without your support, and know that every message, every interaction, every feedback we got has [b]really made a difference, has kept us going, has shown us the way forward,[/b] and we can only [b]hope that you will love the game, as much as we loved making it! (so far!)[/b] Until the next one Void Hunters!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/b59ee068423a08c66b49b83b7fe9d8fb7853a631.gif[/img]

[b][i]~ Soulstone Survivors team[/i][/b]

[h3]Greetings, Void Hunters![/h3]

[b]Hotfix 3 for Update 16: The Titan Hunt[/b] is now live! Once again thanks to your help and feedback we identified and solve another batch of issues big and small with the new content added to the game! Here's a list of all thats changed in this update:

[h2]General fixes and improvements:[/h2]
[list]
[*]Spider Cocoon reworked: the cocoon explosion now deals damage and applies Weakness, but summons only a single explosive spiderling that applies Bleed once its duration ends. Spiderlings are now capped at 14 active simultaneously, but will count as regular summons, giving you benefits for skills that scale off of quantity of summons, for example. Damage has also been considerably increased to compensate for the change;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Egg Hunt special event would not work as intended when completed, possibly leading to a black screen when entering the portal;
[*]Fixed Volcanic Eruption, Volcanic Effigy and Fiery Blades that, when combined with Radiance, would cause the game to break;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Player icon would disappear from the minimap;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Sentinel's ascension would not work properly when using the Corrupted skin;
[*]Fixed an issue wher Bloody Saw would not cause damage in the area it was supposed to;
[*]Fixed an issue where Skill Affinity runes could be triggered twice in Titan Hunt mode;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Home portal would appear too early, possibly causing it to not work;
[*]Fixed an issue where multiple UI elements would not become invisible during boss presentations;
[*]Fixed an issue where the ending screen would show the incorrect Sigil information in the Titan Hunt;
[*]Fixed an issue where Aruanak's attacks (Spider titan) would become invisible with very low effect visibility settings;
[*]Fixed an issue where the character art would not be displayed properly in the Profile screen;
[*]Fixed multiple minor issues that would cause log spam in the background, which could cause performance issues;
[/list]

We continue working on your feedback and if you run into any issues with this update please do let us know! There are still a few errors we are chasing but we hope that this update will make your overall experience considerably smoother! As always we wanted to thank you for your amazing support, and we hope you are enjoying the Titan Hunt!

[img]{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/42629950/0613ae8b16cc071c726ac24a6c6e0f9156b2c8a2.gif[/img]

[i][b]~ Soulstone Survivors team[/b][/i]

[h3]Greetings, Void Hunters![/h3]

We have just released [b]Hotfix 2 for Update 16: The Titan Hunt![/b] We have been keeping an eye on your feedback, and have fixed quite a few errors! We had another Hotfix update last night so we thought we would consolidate all of the fixes in these first couple of days in a single announcement!

[h2]General fixes and improvements:[/h2]
[list]
[*]Considerably reduced health of Titans and overall scaling of first 5 cycles of the Titan Hunt;
[*]Considerably reduced damage and increased cooldown of a few Titan abilities, such as Mhyzahet's Tornadoes, Aruanak's Web Shot and other overtuned skills;
[*]Fixed an issue with the Kobold Sparkies intro animation, which could cause Vyvolt to be teleported out of the map;
[*]Fixed an issue where multiple Shaman achievements were unlocking the incorrect skill;
[*]Fixed an issue where Fiery Blades would not be able to hit Tentacles;
[*]Fixed an issue where it would be possible to trigger the Kobold Sparkies fight while outside of the boss arena, causing the game to soft-lock;
[*]Fixed an issue where the achievement of completing the Ritual of Hate was not possible to complete, making the Demon Hunter impossible to unlock;
[*]Made it so bonus events such as Chests and Massive Minerals spawn a bit earlier in the Void Fields;
[*]Fixed an issue where in very high levels, skills such as Shadow Spikes might not hit all enemies correctly;
[*]Fixed an issue where if you selected the Shaman while it was unlocked, it would show the Barbarian skin doing something weird;
[*]Fixed an issue where the Myrmidon's size would be smaller while her ascension was active;
[*]Fixed an issue where multiple static skills (like totems) would not show that they benefit from Critical Chance power ups (visual issue only);
[*]Addressed an issue where the new Corrupted skins would show a placeholder description, still not the final fix but better than before;
[*]Fixed an issue where it was possible to start another task in the Titan Hunt after you had collected all necessary Void Fragments, possibly causing the game to soft-lock;
[*]Fixed multiple small issues that would cause a spam of errors in the background, affecting performance (harmless errors);
[*]Fixed an issue where some of the new Corrupted skins would not properly show their character's intro animations;
[*]Fixed an issue where it would be possible to have a sticky tooltip being fixed on screen permanently while using a controller;
[*]Fixed an issue where Living Weapon would not benefit from your runes and possibly cause exceptions leading to weird behaviour;
[*]Fixed an issue where Soulstone icons could stay permanently on the minimap, even after they were collected;
[*]Replaced Shaman's ascension Spirit Guide model with a new model. [i][b]Developer note:[/b] We sometimes buy assets from asset stores to speed up development. We mostly use these assets as a starting point to create our own models; unfortunately in this case it seems the model we used as base is very similar to a character from another IP. We were not aware of this and are actively working to make the Shaman's ascension more unique, yet still inspired by Quetzalcoatl, the Mayan God, as intended. Today we replaced the model with a new one created on top of Mayan sculptures to be as true as we can to our inspiration, and we are creating new animations as we speak, which will come in our next hotfix update.[/i]
[/list]

We hope that the fixes above make your experience smoother, and as always we wanted to thank you for your amazing support! Your feedback and bug reports are, as always, essential to make the game better, so thank you for taking the time to write us!

We hope you are enjoying the update and... [b]happy hunting![/b]

